protocol "PBM — Cognitive Enhancement 1064nm" {
    id: "30000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
    description: "Right prefrontal 1064nm PBM, approximating the acute cognitive literature (Gonzalez-Lima / Barrett lineage: 0.25 W/cm² CW, 60 J/cm²/site, 8 min). NOT YET EVIDENCE-GRADE, for two independent reasons: (1) DUTY — this channel's duty cycle is firmware-capped at 25% (np_pbm1064_drive_set_duty(), cannot be raised by any session parameter), so true CW is not achievable; delivered average irradiance is ~0.10 W/cm² vs. the literature's 0.25 W/cm² CW — a 2.5× shortfall. (2) DOSE — firmware limits this channel to 36 J/cm²/session (OI-SES-01), well below the literature's 60 J/cm²/site. (3) AREA — the treated zone (8 modules, ~111 cm²) is ~8.2× the literature's single-site aperture (~13.6 cm²), because precisely naming the 1–2 modules over Fp2/F4 depends on gate REG-1 (10-20 socket registration), still open. 'Grade A' / gold-standard wording is withheld until REG-1 lands and the zone is re-authored to the true footprint — the duty/dose shortfall (1)-(2) is a separate, still-open gap that re-authoring alone will not close. See docs/status/pending-decisions.md §13.2c."
    author: "NeurOne"
    version: "1.1"
    readonly: true
    tags: ["pbm", "1064nm", "clinical", "cognition"]
    conditions: ["Mild Cognitive Impairment"]
    references: [["PBM protocol database §3 (literature is Grade A; NeurOne delivery does not yet match — see gate note)", "docs/pbm_neuro_protocols.md#3-cognitive-enhancement--healthy-adults--cognitive-aging--grade-a"], ["Gonzalez-Lima / Barrett lineage", "docs/pbm_neuro_protocols.md"], ["Lateralization decision + optical model", "docs/np_opt_psf_001.md"], ["Evidence-grade claim gate + firmware duty/dose ceiling", "docs/status/pending-decisions.md#132c-clinical-03-dose-fidelity-gap"]]
    duration: 8m

    pbm_transcranial {
        intensity: 100%
        frequency: 0Hz
        duty_cycle: 25%
        # duty_cycle: 25% is the firmware-enforced ceiling for this channel
        # (np_pbm1064_drive_set_duty(), NP-FW-PBM1064-001 §5) — not a session
        # choice, and cannot be raised from here. True continuous-wave output at
        # literature intensity (0.25 W/cm²) is not achievable on current hardware;
        # this delivers ~0.10 W/cm² average, within the 36 J/cm²/session ceiling
        # (OI-SES-01), which is itself below the literature's 60 J/cm²/site dose.
        # frequency: 0Hz selects the closest available mode (no periodic
        # entrainment); it does not mean this reaches literature CW output.
        # "Frontal Right" includes midline sockets 1/5/13, which put ~50% of their
        # cortical energy contralateral — 16.3% of the whole zone's, in a protocol whose
        # entire evidence base is right-lateralized. Narrowed per PR #210's ruling
        # (dis-inclusion = author a narrower zone). See docs/np_opt_psf_001.md §4.
        zones: ["Frontal Right (excl. midline)"]
        wavelength: 1064nm
    }
}
